<speak>He is learning, and I am learning to let him do things differently. That is probably the harder part. When he changes a routine, I instinctively ask why, because I remember how it was done before. Sometimes there is a good reason for the old way, but sometimes we simply kept doing it. I am trying to spend less time hovering over every task. My brother says I cannot ask the younger generation to take responsibility and then stand behind them correcting the position of every folder. He is right, although he used to do exactly the same thing when he was managing the warehouse.</speak>